{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions","id":482305,"title":"Swaggering VS Submissive conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T07:39:49-07:00","id":482305,"title":"Swaggering VS Submissive conditions","content":"For comparison:<br /> <br /> <b>Swaggering:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence.<br /> He\u2019s sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu\u2019s fury. He<br /> can not prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any<br /> way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal<br /> routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making<br /> an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may<br /> make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional<br /> point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal<br /> to the Rahu\u2019s Purity.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Possible Sources: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The Rahu\u2019s Dominant hunter aspect.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Resolution: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Suffer a wound penalty from lethal or aggravated<br /> wounds, or suffer a lethal wound in your character\u2019s<br /> last Health box.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Beat: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">n/a</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Submissive:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence.<br /> He\u2019s cowed, and cannot bear to face the Rahu\u2019s fury. He can<br /> not directly attack, insult, or defy the Rahu, or the Rahu\u2019s<br /> pack, without first spending a Willpower point and making<br /> an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may<br /> make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional<br /> point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal<br /> to the Rahu\u2019s Purity. You don\u2019t need to spend Willpower or<br /> roll if the Rahu or one of her pack has attacked your character<br /> this turn.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Possible Sources: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The Rahu\u2019s Dominant hunter aspect.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Resolution: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Suffer a wound penalty from lethal or aggravated<br /> wounds, or suffer a lethal wound in your character\u2019s<br /> last Health box.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Beat: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">n/a</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I like Swaggering better. Submissive is simply boring. It ends the fight. By the time that the condition is resolved by itself, the character would be dead. Swaggering, on the other hand, allows for different outcomes, while still putting your prey right where the Rahu wants it: in a straight up brawl. Furthermore, Rahu aren't default alphas who'd apply Submissive to the first hint of dissent from their packmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:42:25-07:00","id":482325,"title":"","content":"Swaggering is thematically inappropriate. That's not the kind of behavior a Rahu promotes.<br /> Maybe if they had named it something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:59:49-07:00","id":482334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482325#post482325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swaggering is thematically inappropriate. That's not the kind of behavior a Rahu promotes.<br /> Maybe if they had named it something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. The condition was changed deliberately to bring it into line with the Auspice's description of the Rahu hunter's aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahu writeup</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter\u2019s Aspect: Dominant. The prey spoils for a fight. He has no idea that death is coming, he thinks he can win<br /> this. He sees the movement in the shadow as nothing he can\u2019t handle, and goes in search of satisfaction \u2014 mating, food, good company.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:17:20-07:00","id":482376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482334#post482334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is. The condition was changed deliberately to bring it into line with the Auspice's description of the Rahu hunter's aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Hunter Aspect makes sense in the first place. The Rahu should be expressing his dominance, not make other people feel dominant or foolish. The flavor text of the Rahu does spend a paragraph discussing that not every Rahu is moral paragon, and can resort to devious and underhanded tricks, but that paragraph seems designed to widen the variety of Rahu characters someone can play. It does not seem to suggest that every Rahu defaults to devious and underhanded tricks.<br /> <br /> I wrote this minor change over in the other thread. I feel that it fits much better.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Challenged</b></u><br /> <b>Your character has been called out by the force of a Rahu's essence. He has been encouraged or shamed into immediately facing this challenge.</b> He cannot prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal to the Rahu's Purity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:25:36-07:00","id":482392,"title":"","content":"I (naturally) disagree. When you lay a hunter's aspect on a prey, you're saying &quot;this hunt will go the way that works best for my Auspice&quot;. For the Rahu, having the prey reduced to a snivelling wreck doesn't tie in to that. Having the prey flush with false bravado only to be proved wrong when his limbs come off in the werewolf's jaws ties in much closer. The hunter's aspect sets up the situation that will end with the Rahu's prey dominated (or probably dead), rather than just being the Cahalith's aspect turned up a notch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:37:47-07:00","id":482411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482392#post482392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hunter's aspect sets up the situation that will end with the Rahu's prey dominated (or probably dead), rather than just being the Cahalith's aspect turned up a notch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it sets up a situation that will end with the Rahu's prey dominated, but several instances of flavor text in the Rahu section alone discuss how the Rahu <b>&quot;unlike the Irraka, who would prefer to kill his prey before the prey knows what is happening, the Rahu wants the prey to know that it is dying and why.&quot;</b> and <b>&quot;tries to \u201cwin\u201d conversations rather than coming to consensus. Friendly physical games often become painful as the full-moon brings her full skill to bear. Insults, meant in jest or not, come back to the speaker with renewed venom. The Rahu will not be bested except by a worthy opponent.&quot;</b> and <b>&quot;They are stubborn and headstrong by nature&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> None of that thematically suggests that every Rahu fools or tricks their prey into feeling overconfident.<br /> I definitely agree that the mechanics of Swaggering are much better than Submissive!<br /> But the flavor text does not fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:49:26-07:00","id":482427,"title":"","content":"I think it fits. You're not going to win against someone who just gives up. Swagger gives them the confidence to stand up to the rahu, to their regret.<br /> <br /> Especially as a hunter's aspect, with the rahu coming out in some wicked form, people have little reason to stick around when confronted by a true warrior Uratha. It's like an extension of call out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:56:38-07:00","id":482432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482427#post482427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like an extension of call out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not calling them out. It's fooling them into thinking they can win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:58:31-07:00","id":482434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482432#post482432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not calling them out. It's fooling them into thinking they can win.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If they don't think they could win, why would they fight a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:09:44-07:00","id":482445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482434#post482434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't think they could win, why would they fight a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because their pride is on the line, because they would be shamed if they did not, because they still think it is their best chance, because they want to protect something they love, because they want to distract the werewolf while their friends escape, because their friends are already in the fight, because they think the consequences for losing are not bad, because you want to <i>really hurt</i> the damn thing before you go down, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:13:39-07:00","id":482447,"title":"","content":"You don't think you'd need confidence to think distracting a werewolf to let your friends escape or that one extra hand in a fight against a werewolf that might be healing all damage every few seconds? Or that you'd even have a chance to hurt it? Or to balance shame over certain death?<br /> <br /> And while those might be the case for humans, though I doubt it in the face of something that can shift into gauru form, do you think a spirit is going to care about shame? A claimed about pride, provided it isn't claimed by a pride spirit? A beshilu about consequences? A vampire about something they love, balanced against their potential immortality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-16-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:24:27-07:00","id":482455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482447#post482447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think you'd need confidence to think distracting a werewolf to let your friends escape or that one extra hand in a fight against a werewolf that might be healing all damage every few seconds? Or that you'd even have a chance to hurt it? Or to balance shame over certain death?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Werewolves do not turn into Gauru every single fight. If we're talking about a human then many of your fights are going to be in Dalu or Hishu. If we're talking about animals then how much confidence does a mama bear really need to defend her cubs from an Urshul or Urhan? If we're talking about aggressive spirits then how much confidence do they need to follow their nature?<br /> <br /> 2) There is a big difference between standing up to someone, and being fooled into thinking there is no chance you could possibly lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:29:00-07:00","id":482456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482455#post482455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Werewolves do not turn into Gauru every single fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we're talking about a human then many of your fights are going to be in Dalu or Hishu. If we're talking about animals then how much confidence does a mama bear really need to defend her cubs from an Urshul or Urhan? If we're talking about aggressive spirits then how much confidence do they need to follow their nature? </div> </div> </div>Not really, dalu, urhan hishu are hunting and hiding forms. Urshul and Gauru are the fighting forms. And even with dalu you're gaining half a foot on top of your regular height and have access to the 'Badass Motherfucker' ability because you appear like a Badass Motherfucker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:39:42-07:00","id":482467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482456#post482456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, dalu, urhan hishu are hunting and hiding forms. Urshul and Gauru are the fighting forms. And even with dalu you're gaining half a foot on top of your regular height and have access to the 'Badass Motherfucker' ability because you appear like a Badass Motherfucker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you suggesting that most of your human combats are going to involve you turning into Urshul or Gauru?<br /> I'm not certain if that is what you are saying, but it seems like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:51:55-07:00","id":482478,"title":"","content":"Indeed... I find that my Cahalith character fights FAR more often in Hishu form than any other, especially when his opponents are Human. No Need to shapeshift, after all, to put a Human in its place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:56:39-07:00","id":482485,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with Swaggering, I like the mechanics and I think it makes sense as a Condition the Rahu would place on their prey. Besides, I thought Submissive and Resigned were to conceptually similar and stepped on each other's toes anyway.<br /> <br /> But I don't like &quot;Dominant&quot; as the name of the Hunter's Aspect that causes Swaggering. It makes sense that a monstrous presence would make you feel resigned to your fate. It makes sense that an isolating presence would make you feel alone and helpless. It makes sense that a mystifying presence would leave you in fear of the strange and mysterious. It makes sense that a deceptively blissful presence would leave you ignorant of the fact that you're being hunted. It makes sense that a dominant presence would make you feel submissive, but not so much that it would make you overconfident or swaggering.<br /> <br /> I'd rather the Hunter's Aspect be called Challenging or something similar. Instead of trying to dominate the prey, the Rahu calls it out. It's Hunter's Aspect says &quot;come at me without any of your fancy tools. Let's go, just me and you.&quot; And the prey can't help but accept the challenge. Or, it can, but it costs Willpower and an extended Resolve + Composure roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:56:57-07:00","id":482486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482467#post482467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you suggesting that most of your human combats are going to involve you turning into Urshul or Gauru?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we just talking about fighting now? Because hunter's aspect isn't a fighting style. And the frequency of your shapeshifts to combat and what you fight in really has no bearing on any of it, since it's going to work on a table to table basis. 100% of my fights with humans have been in urshul or gauru form. Plus you're neglecting everything that is not human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:18:06-07:00","id":482506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482486#post482486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we just talking about fighting now? Because hunter's aspect isn't a fighting style. And the frequency of your shapeshifts to combat and what you fight in really has no bearing on any of it, since it's going to work on a table to table basis</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about fighting.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482486#post482486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't think they could win, why would they fight a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482486#post482486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">100% of my fights with humans have been in urshul or gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean no disrespect when I say this, but I think this is a minority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:25:12-07:00","id":482510,"title":"","content":"You're talking more about direct combat. I probably should have used the term confront.<br /> <br /> And still, your examples rely on a certain type of human in a certain type of situation that is just as likely to be the minority of encounters with a rahu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:30:37-07:00","id":482513,"title":"","content":"So, You &quot;Confront&quot; your Human opponents in Urshul or Gauru 100% of the time when fighting? Really? Seems a bit..... odd to me, I think. Kinda stand out in a Bar Brawl do you? So much for not alerting the Herd to the Werewolf existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:39:39-07:00","id":482542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482510#post482510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably should have used the term confront.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would have saved us a detour. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482510#post482510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And still, your examples rely on a certain type of human in a certain type of situation that is just as likely to be the minority of encounters with a rahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly at this point I'm not sure where you're going with this. The thrust of my point was that fooling someone else into extreme overconfidence is not consistent with the majority of flavor presented about Rahu in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T11:03:33-07:00","id":482583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482542#post482542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly at this point I'm not sure where you're going with this. The thrust of my point was that fooling someone else into extreme overconfidence is not consistent with the majority of flavor presented about Rahu in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because the rahu are warriors, and a warrior fights 'because it is right to do so.' This is brought out in their opponents, this makes the rahu have a fight and not a slaughter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T11:24:20-07:00","id":482596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482583#post482583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because the rahu are warriors, and a warrior fights 'because it is right to do so.' This is brought out in their opponents, this makes the rahu have a fight and not a slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swaggering doesn't make enemies fight you 'because it is right to do so'. Swaggering makes the combat more likely to be a slaughter than a fair combat. Swaggering fools the enemy, which is design space already represented in other areas.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T11:32:38-07:00","id":482605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482334#post482334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is. The condition was changed deliberately to bring it into line with the Auspice's description of the Rahu hunter's aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give us a scenario of how that would make sense for the Purity auspice? It seems very Cunning right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:30:12-07:00","id":482637,"title":"","content":"The Challenging re-name sounds most promising, at least to me. I mean, the Rahu is all about the &quot;Come at me Bro&quot; mind-set, so forcing the opponent in to a rash, confrontational and all or nothing condition works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:55:26-07:00","id":482650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482605#post482605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give us a scenario of how that would make sense for the Purity auspice? It seems very Cunning right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prey: So what happens now?<br /> <br /> Rahu: We face each other as God intended. Sportsman-like. No tricks. No weapons. Skill against skill alone.<br /> <br /> Prey: You mean... You put down your rock and I'll put down my sword and... We'll try and kill each other like civilized people?<br /> <br /> Rahu: Or I can kill you now.<br /> <br /> Prey: *putting down sword* Frankly, I think the odds are slightly in your favor at hand-fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-16-2015, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T14:37:01-07:00","id":482823,"title":"","content":"Would that not be in the Prey's Favor, <i><b>Charlaquin</b></i>? After all, he should be confident of his abilities and that he will win, assuming condition is in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:11:11-07:00","id":482961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482823#post482823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not be in the Prey's Favor, <i><b>Charlaquin</b></i>? After all, he should be confident of his abilities and that he will win, assuming condition is in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't know that confidence is strictly necessary. As long as the prey feels urged to rise to the challenge, be that due to overconfidence, social pressure, or what have you. Some of the accuracy of my example had to be sacrificed for the sake of the reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-16-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:03:22-07:00","id":483072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=482650#post482650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prey: So what happens now?<br /> <br /> Rahu: We face each other as God intended. Sportsman-like. No tricks. No weapons. Skill against skill alone.<br /> <br /> Prey: You mean... You put down your rock and I'll put down my sword and... We'll try and kill each other like civilized people?<br /> <br /> Rahu: Or I can kill you now.<br /> <br /> Prey: *putting down sword* Frankly, I think the odds are slightly in your favor at hand-fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think that is a great example of Purity and what a Rahu is all about. But the prey doesn't seem to have the swaggering condition as written, unless he is lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T20:14:57-07:00","id":483129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=483072#post483072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think that is a great example of Purity and what a Rahu is all about. But the prey doesn't seem to have the swaggering condition as written, unless he is lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, accuracy had to be sacrificed for the sake of the reference. If Fezik had actually been a Rahu, Westly probably would have been much more enthusiastic about the idea. Also, Fezik would probably have won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T21:53:28-07:00","id":483163,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> Westley was the Rahu. The Prey was <i>Vizzini</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't compete with you physically, and you're no match for my brains.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:02:31-07:00","id":483221,"title":"","content":"Westley,very clearly, can't be the werewolf here.<br /> <br /> Where's his pack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T00:55:49-07:00","id":483332,"title":"","content":"My 2c<br /> <br /> If you've ever seen two drunks rile each other up and let it escalate into fisty-cuffs I think that kind of bravado osmosis is precisely how I picture swagger working. It's not that one is tricking the other, just that its infectious - rising to the challenge is very much a natural response. <br /> <br /> It's just that I this case one (or both) of those participants happens to be a werewolf who does it all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":2721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","user":"Elkovash","date":". 04-17-2015, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T02:13:52-07:00","id":483365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=483332#post483332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've ever seen two drunks rile each other up and let it escalate into fisty-cuffs I think that kind of bravado osmosis is precisely how I picture swagger working. It's not that one is tricking the other, just that its infectious - rising to the challenge is very much a natural response.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be the best explanation I have seen for it so far. One guy bellowing at the other guy to 'Come At Me Bro' or a suitably dramatic equivalent, while the opponent feeds off the energy of the <b>challenge</b> and is goaded into battle.<br /> <br /> But the fluff of swaggering doesn't really suggest rising to a challenge, but instead being convinced that you cannot possibly lose.<br /> Which is why several of us have been suggesting the fluff be changed to represent a challenge, or at least the name changed from Dominant to Challenging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T03:57:57-07:00","id":483397,"title":"","content":"You can't really be dominating and make someone feel the need to recklessly fight you. I mean, I suppose you could be so smug that someone wants to make you swallow teeth, but smug isn't really a Rahu kind of thing. You can be challenging; using your voice and body language to inspire someone to rise to the challenge, and commit recklessly to a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T05:17:45-07:00","id":483434,"title":"","content":"I think it really comes down to the person on the receiving end. Some people will just cow to it without a fight, but others will see someone getting too big for their britches and possibly read it as empty posturing.<br /> <br /> Of course, having one aspect result in different conditions depending on who it hits would break the symmetry so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:04:04-07:00","id":483518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=483221#post483221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Westley,very clearly, can't be the werewolf here.<br /> <br /> Where's his pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>He is a Pack of One... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:20:57-07:00","id":483611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions?p=483221#post483221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Westley,very clearly, can't be the werewolf here.<br /> <br /> Where's his pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a pirate captain. He's got a crew.<br /> <br /> Also, Auspice Benefit: &quot;Perhaps I have the strength after all.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:04:00-07:00","id":489622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/482305-swaggering-vs-submissive-conditions#post482305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For comparison:<br /> <br /> <b>Swaggering:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence.<br /> He\u2019s sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu\u2019s fury. He<br /> can not prepare himself to face the Rahu or her pack in any<br /> way \u2014 buying weapons, laying traps, or changing his normal<br /> routine \u2014 without first spending a Willpower point and making<br /> an extended, reflexive Resolve + Composure roll. You may<br /> make one roll per turn, but each roll requires an additional<br /> point of Willpower. The target number of successes is equal<br /> to the Rahu\u2019s Purity.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Possible Sources: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The Rahu\u2019s Dominant hunter aspect.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Resolution: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Suffer a wound penalty from lethal or aggravated<br /> wounds, or suffer a lethal wound in your character\u2019s<br /> last Health box.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Beat: </b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">n/a</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just a matter of re-wording: <br /> <br /> <b>Your character faced the full bore of a Rahu\u2019s essence.<i> Instead of being intimidated he\u2019s has become cocky and overconfident</i> and is sure that he can win in the face of the Rahu's fury.</b><br /> <br /> I feel that this isn't so much a matter of the Rahu causing the prey to feel overconfident as it is the prey is already confident, and sensing the Rahu's Dominant presence makes them overcompensate, which can be a deadly mistake in a Rahu's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","user":"Nuwisha Nutjob","date":". 04-23-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}